{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790254833,"nonce":"xgjiO3OT+C/FS++9uosmeNb+Jjk=","title":"Lua: os.time(t) normalizes fields into t that the types never see","message":"os.time(t) stores year, month, day, hour, min, sec, wday, yday and isdst into the table it is given (zl_date_table_fill), but the typer does not record those stores against t's shape. A name the constructor did not write (min, sec, wday, yday, isdst) is then typed absent: field_read_ty gives the metatable chain's type, nil for a plain table.\n\nReproducer: local t = {year = 2000, month = 13, day = 40, hour = 25}; os.time(t); print(t.min, t.wday). Main prints the values because the read of a name outside the shape takes the general path; a lowering that trusts an absent name to be nil (a closed lookup) prints nil. The same applies to a class or __index table handed to os.time: an instance read of min through the chain is typed as the chain's type without min.\n\nFix: model os.time's argument as stores of Int under the eight date names and Bool under isdst in the typer (next to rawset in metatable_builtin), so the shape gains the fields as slots.","files":null}]}